# @NAME@

This application can build on its own using the installed Umicom Framework SDK.
The same repository can be registered below `applications/@SLUG@` in the Umicom
Applications suite. Registration uses Git; copying a folder does not register it.

## Build independently

1. Install the Umicom Framework development package and a C23 compiler, CMake
   and Ninja. For the GTK4 frontend, also install GTK4 and pkg-config.
2. Open PowerShell in this directory. Replace the SDK prefix with your installation.
3. Run each command separately and stop if it fails.

```powershell
cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="C:/umicom/installed/applications" -DBUILD_TESTING=ON
cmake --build build --parallel 2
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure --no-tests=error
cmake --install build --prefix "C:/umicom/installed/@SLUG@"
```

For a console build, pass `-DUMICOM_@IDENTIFIER@_BUILD_GTK4=OFF` when configuring.
On Windows, launch `.\build\@CONSOLE_EXECUTABLE@.exe Contributor`.
When the GTK4 frontend is enabled, launch `.\build\umicom-@SLUG@.exe`.
On Linux use the same executable paths without `.exe`.

A successful console run prints a greeting. The model and console tests must
both pass. A compiler or missing-SDK error is not a test result. If CMake cannot
find UmicomFramework, check that the SDK prefix contains its CMake package and
headers, then configure again. To change compilers, choose a new build directory.

## Add to a suite

1. Review and publish this repository using your normal Git workflow.
2. In your suite checkout, run `git submodule add <your-repository-url> applications/@SLUG@`.
3. Read this module's identity with `umicom repo inspect-module applications/@SLUG@/application.umicom.yaml`.
4. Enable the build option printed by that command at the next suite configure.
5. Build and test before publishing the parent repository's submodule pointer.

The Framework discovery helper creates the build option and reuses this
module's tests and installer rules. It does not generate an application launcher
entry or a product-specific shared workstation controller. The optional GTK
window is owned by this module.

## Extend the application

Keep rules in the model and display code in the frontends. The generated tests
cover validation and output bounds. Expand them whenever behaviour changes.
See `docs/application-features.md` for the supported feature list.

Creation writes source only. No repository is committed, no remote is created,
and no existing suite is changed. If creation fails, inspect any retained
partial directory and choose a fresh destination; existing files are never
overwritten on retry.
